  "worked_solution": "We find the total displacement by calculating the definite integral of the velocity.\n\nLet $d$ be the total displacement between $t=3$ and $t=4.$ Then we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & ={\\int }_{3}^{4}(16-9{t}^{2})\\,\\text{dt} \\\\  & ={(16t-3{t}^{3})|}_{3}^{4} \\\\  & =[16(4)-3(4)^{3}]-[16(3)-3(3)^{3}] \\\\  & =[64-192]-[48-81] \\\\  & =-95.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
